From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:21:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 46/54] blitz-dom: a scroll comes to rest at its snap position
 (CSS Scroll Snap)

scroll_snap.rs picks the snap position a scroll comes to rest at, from
scroll-snap-type, scroll-snap-align, scroll-snap-stop and scroll-padding:
mandatory and proximity (a third of the snapport), start, end and center,
areas longer than the snapport valid wherever they cover it, unreachable
positions clamped to the scroll range (below zero for a scroller whose
content overflows the other way), and the intent of the scroll
(ScrollSnapIntent: end position, into view, direction, page).

scroll_to snaps as an end position, scroll_by as a direction,
scroll_into_view keeps its element in view, and a scrollbar thumb let go
snaps. scroll_to_with_snap and scroll_snap_position let an embedder say
what a scroll meant, or that it has not come to rest yet (a wheel gesture
under way). User scrolls through scroll_chain_by do not snap.

Needs Stylo with these properties in Servo mode, behind
`layout.css.scroll-snap.enabled`, which init_stylo_prefs sets.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
